{
  "reviews": [
    {
      "actor": "ash-1",
      "decision": "reuse",
      "ability": "root-air-drying",
      "reason": "The implemented root-air-drying capability already provides the requested physical preservation function: actual roots are processed on a reusable tray, lose water under suitable weather, and receive reversible preservation only while sufficiently dry. It requires real materials, effort and individual learning; neither equipment nor preserved food is supplied by this review. Current inventory shows two remaining roots with accumulated decay 18.72304092, rather than the three recorded before the recent meal. Missing equipment does not require a different capability.",
      "specification": "Reuse roots:weather-air-drying:1 unchanged; consult root-air-drying for its full public operation schema, shared reference parameters, geometry, preservation multiplier and safety thresholds before execution. Learning requires four simulation rounds. Building reserves two actual stone units and one bark and requires two rounds at one energy per round. Loading accepts up to two original root units; raw roots require two crushing rounds per root at one energy per round. Use the existing contract for already-crushed inputs. Uncovered drying requires dry weather at 10–40 C and removes at most 0.005 water mass per original root per round toward water fraction 0.12; rain can restore up to 0.01 per original root per round, bounded by original water content. Retain actual food composition, nutrition, toxicity, provenance and accumulated spoilage: drying does not reset age, restore spoiled food or certify indefinite safety. Validate actual ownership, accessibility and shared tray geometry. Preserve the registered process's remaining work, pause, maintenance, removal and cancellation behavior; death must cancel actor work without duplicating or deleting escrow or tray contents. No simulation time passes during this review.",
      "experienceReview": "Reuse existing feedback rather than register an alias. Completed, paid processing can emit practice-confirmed on root-air-drying only at its existing qualified milestones with real changed outputs: personal amount 0.4, cap 0.5, duration 8, refresh cooldown 12; maintained gain 0.02 and decay 0.001 under the registered rule. Mastery, requests and mere process inspection do not qualify. A performed experiment that actually confirms new preservation information may separately emit information-confirmed through probe under grounded-understanding: amount 0.8, cap 1, duration 8, refresh cooldown 12, maintained gain 0.035 and decay 0.0015; repeated known facts do not qualify. These represent limited grounded progress and understanding, not achievement accumulation. Eating the actual output uses existing meal-experience feedback based on consumed composition, realized nutrition and quality, without a second preservation pleasure bonus. Physical nutrition, toxicity and survival remain independent.",
      "visualReview": "Use the existing tray and food rendering at their actual shared-world positions, with visible contents, processing progress, water fraction, accumulated spoilage and current drying or rewetting status. Bind replay and inspection to drying-tray-built, food-drying-progress, food-drying-completed, food-rewetted, process-inspected and applicable process-progress, process-completed and process-stopped events. Show preservation only when the real moisture-dependent condition holds; do not display an unearned safety, freshness or completion badge. Experience subscriptions remain practice-confirmed, information-confirmed and meal-experience, with their registered qualification checks.",
      "learning": 4
    }
  ]
}

